  "historical_output_text": " A few paragraphs are all needed, not exceeding 5.\n\nIt wasn´t a day of grand epiphones so often herald when I first noticed my car’s tire-pressure monitor flashing a red “check”. The alarm rang in early as I pulled in the morning and again late in a doldral afternoon when work had ended. A routine check and fill-up revealed one side had dropped, not enough that I noticed until I was stopped. A quick visit home and some dry ice and my problem resolved.\n\nIt's not the first such incident with the system. It seems a part is failing on my vehicle; a minor nuisance in itself as it only goes to remind me the occasional need and effort it can be worth it. It did give a pause as it made me reflect upon how we are always so quick to assume a system fails because of an obvious",
